Could be a spoiler... 
Experience has taught me that the back way is the best.  Why?
(1) You can fight the monsters one-on-one in the narrow passageway behind
    the throne room;
(2) If you get in trouble, you can always back up and let them take a
    one-way trip to hell through the trapdoors (lots of fun to watch);
(3) If you want to tangle with four dragons (two at a time), you can raid the
    four storerooms before the assault...and possibly make that dragon scale
    mail you've been waiting for, along with munching dragons for intrinsics.
Also, for adventurers with guts, this way none of the monsters can run away
from you...for long.
Incidentally, a ROC helps a LOT in the castle!
